1
00:00:00,680 --> 00:00:02,977
One Dream,

2
00:00:08,420 --> 00:00:15,420
oh.

3
00:00:49,860 --> 00:00:52,660
Thank you.

4
00:01:15,720 --> 00:01:22,120
Thank you so much for watching.

5
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:39,980
Oh, what's the top?

6
00:01:46,820 --> 00:01:48,880
You should go Stussy elsewhere.

7
00:01:49,260 --> 00:01:52,436
You are aware of who controls
this country, I presume.

8
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:55,540
It looked like I'd give a crap.

9
00:01:55,720 --> 00:01:56,880
It's Kaido, right?

10
00:01:57,140 --> 00:01:58,400
Tell him we're here!

11
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:01,740
To take down an emperor!

12
00:02:02,060 --> 00:02:03,236
Dial it back, Luffy.

13
00:02:03,960 --> 00:02:06,254
Kin'emon said we're supposed to lay low.

14
00:02:07,440 --> 00:02:09,780
Oh, I was just kidding!

15
00:02:10,620 --> 00:02:11,450
Sorry!

16
00:02:19,360 --> 00:02:21,557
Let's see what the cards have to say about

17
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:24,346
the probability of you
surviving a month here.

18
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,877
A firm 19%.

19
00:02:30,960 --> 00:02:31,960
Hmm.

20
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:35,617
That's an interesting sword you got there.

21
00:02:35,700 --> 00:02:37,935
Where the heck did you get that thing?

22
00:02:39,060 --> 00:02:41,236
It's a Fancy Pants Famous one, right?

23
00:02:45,380 --> 00:02:48,577
Well, if it is what I think
it is, it's a powerful one.

24
00:02:48,660 --> 00:02:51,072
You should probably let me hold on to it.

25
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:55,030
No way.

26
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:57,037
You don't even know how to use it.

27
00:02:57,120 --> 00:02:58,649
Now hand it over, come on.

28
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:02,000
I'ma slash them up good. Killed them.

29
00:03:08,120 --> 00:03:10,500
Let's see what this thing can do!

30
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:14,100
Don't throw the scabbard, Luffy!

31
00:03:18,460 --> 00:03:20,240
Now come go!

32
00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:22,470
Pistol!

33
00:03:23,520 --> 00:03:26,200
You're not using it right!

34
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:32,140
Even the lizard's biting me!

35
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:35,700
Hey, knock it off!

36
00:03:43,980 --> 00:03:45,540
Straw sword.

37
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:13,340
his sword's creepy I
feel bad for the lizard

38
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:26,100
that was awesome

39
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:56,100
Impressive.

40
00:04:56,860 --> 00:04:58,540
Why is he still standing?

41
00:05:24,280 --> 00:05:25,110
Observe.

42
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:26,860
That's minus one life.

43
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:35,280
You seem confused.

44
00:05:35,620 --> 00:05:39,200
These straw men each represent
the lives of my subordinates.

45
00:05:44,340 --> 00:05:48,620
With my straw straw powers, I can
infuse my body with their spirits.

46
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:50,700
They take damage for me.

47
00:05:51,580 --> 00:05:55,000
If I amass ten souls, I can die ten times.

48
00:06:10,140 --> 00:06:13,720
Now, let's play a game, shall we?

49
00:06:15,180 --> 00:06:16,600
A game?

50
00:06:21,060 --> 00:06:21,890
Here.

51
00:06:21,973 --> 00:06:24,400
We'll let my straw man cards decide.

52
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:40,320
Let's go.

53
00:07:27,480 --> 00:07:31,951
I'm not so bold as to challenge two
members of the worst generation at once.

54
00:07:32,140 --> 00:07:34,375
At least not in a fair fight, that is.

55
00:07:34,700 --> 00:07:37,288
He's a bigger pain in
the ass than he looks.

56
00:07:38,580 --> 00:07:40,180
I should have expected it.

57
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:50,180
Now let us begin.

58
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:05,920
The Fool, reversed.

59
00:08:07,640 --> 00:08:11,280
Drat, this card represents
internal discord.

60
00:08:31,440 --> 00:08:37,497
a shame i'll try to draw a better card
next time despite the risk of a bad draw

61
00:08:37,580 --> 00:08:42,540
there are cards Included that expand one's
ability well beyond its natural limits

62
00:09:10,720 --> 00:09:13,120
Tom, you gotta hang in there.

63
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:15,480
She feels really hot.

64
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:18,172
That must be why her dog is freaking out.

65
00:09:23,220 --> 00:09:24,420
You cowards!

66
00:09:24,580 --> 00:09:25,992
You're not getting away!

67
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:28,889
Hey, Captain, I think
they're getting away!

68
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:35,020
I've drawn a good one.

69
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:42,840
The Hierophant reversed
the card of pursuit.

70
00:10:14,140 --> 00:10:17,080
Hey, Lupi, watch over the brat.

71
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:21,860
Be right back.

72
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:28,480
Won't take long.

73
00:10:30,160 --> 00:10:31,600
I'll handle it.

74
00:10:38,600 --> 00:10:39,600
Thut, thut, thut!

75
00:10:40,660 --> 00:10:41,490
Thut, thut!

76
00:10:41,840 --> 00:10:42,670
Thut!

77
00:11:08,600 --> 00:11:09,760
The hell?

78
00:12:02,720 --> 00:12:04,700
Two-sword style.

79
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:09,200
Nigiri.

80
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:13,520
Tower climb!

81
00:12:15,760 --> 00:12:17,160
Ripple!

82
00:12:46,020 --> 00:12:47,902
Shouldn't we go after them, sir?

83
00:13:01,060 --> 00:13:01,942
The Hierophant.

84
00:13:03,620 --> 00:13:10,180
It's a card of guidance In other words,
a wise figure will lead them to safety

85
00:13:12,320 --> 00:13:14,900
What a pain in my ass

86
00:13:16,660 --> 00:13:19,640
So, what's the status on the brat, Luffy?

87
00:13:24,500 --> 00:13:25,330
Yow!

88
00:13:25,740 --> 00:13:27,400
Tama's really burning up!

89
00:13:27,620 --> 00:13:29,300
Hey, doggie! Hurry!

90
00:13:56,900 --> 00:13:58,420
Hey, why'd you stop?

91
00:14:04,680 --> 00:14:06,417
Are you kidding me?

92
00:14:06,500 --> 00:14:08,280
Did you get us lost?

93
00:14:12,420 --> 00:14:14,820
We don't have a lot of time to waste.

94
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:16,477
Make up your mind.

95
00:14:16,560 --> 00:14:18,100
You want to try right?

96
00:14:20,960 --> 00:14:22,597
I advise left.

97
00:14:22,680 --> 00:14:26,320
You brave samurai are simply
teeming with strength.

98
00:14:27,300 --> 00:14:28,720
Where'd you come from?

99
00:14:31,460 --> 00:14:34,160
It's no easy feat to drive off Hawkins

100
00:14:35,660 --> 00:14:37,020
Who are you?

101
00:14:37,400 --> 00:14:41,640
The woman you saved earlier I
owe you my thanks, Green One

102
00:14:48,280 --> 00:14:50,040
You may call me Tsuru

103
00:14:56,400 --> 00:14:57,230
Hmm

104
00:14:57,900 --> 00:14:59,040
What the hell?

105
00:14:59,380 --> 00:15:02,321
You were hiding in that
dog's tail the whole time?

106
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:04,960
It's true.

107
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:08,860
My gratitude knows no bounds, good sir.

108
00:15:13,020 --> 00:15:14,180
Take this.

109
00:15:15,260 --> 00:15:18,620
Wipe her brow and make that
poor child more comfortable.

110
00:15:19,560 --> 00:15:20,390
Thanks!

111
00:15:21,460 --> 00:15:23,700
I hope this doesn't sound too forward.

112
00:15:24,400 --> 00:15:29,040
However, if it's all right, I insist
that you leave Tama in my care.

113
00:15:29,300 --> 00:15:30,260
You know Tama?

114
00:15:30,800 --> 00:15:31,630
Indeed.

115
00:15:32,900 --> 00:15:33,730
Gotcha.

116
00:15:33,813 --> 00:15:34,643
That'd be great.

117
00:15:35,120 --> 00:15:38,040
You see, she drank dirty river water.

118
00:15:38,140 --> 00:15:41,375
All because she was hungry
and it really messed her up.

119
00:15:41,520 --> 00:15:43,420
Forget the doctor in that case.

120
00:15:44,280 --> 00:15:46,809
We should take her to
my tea house instead.

121
00:15:47,820 --> 00:15:48,650
Tea?

122
00:15:48,733 --> 00:15:50,413
What in the hell are you thinking, lady?

123
00:15:50,680 --> 00:15:53,268
We don't have time for
tea when she's dying.

124
00:15:54,840 --> 00:15:59,134
I don't even know this pipsqueak, but
it's clear that she's in bad shape.

125
00:16:00,820 --> 00:16:01,650
You're right.

126
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,837
But the best remedy to
counteract the river's poison

127
00:16:04,920 --> 00:16:07,685
is a special tea and herb
blends that we carry.

128
00:16:08,580 --> 00:16:11,404
Heed my advice, and she'll
be better in no time.

129
00:16:16,580 --> 00:16:17,440
Okay, then.

130
00:16:17,760 --> 00:16:19,180
I think we should do it.

131
00:16:20,140 --> 00:16:21,060
Thanks a lot.

132
00:16:22,140 --> 00:16:23,800
I still owe you a favor.

133
00:16:25,040 --> 00:16:28,158
I would like to tend to your
injuries, if I may, sir.

134
00:16:51,860 --> 00:16:53,140
For you, sir.

135
00:16:54,260 --> 00:16:56,000
Ah, sweet Tang dumplings.

136
00:16:56,420 --> 00:16:58,891
Nothing I love better from this tea house.

137
00:16:59,580 --> 00:17:01,992
I don't get to eat these as much anymore.

138
00:17:02,980 --> 00:17:04,520
It keeps me going, though.

139
00:17:09,040 --> 00:17:10,680
You say that in jest.

140
00:17:11,860 --> 00:17:16,684
But before you know it, you'll be eating
as many as you wish, just like old times.

141
00:17:17,240 --> 00:17:18,080
Here's hoping.

142
00:17:26,740 --> 00:17:27,820
Hey, geyser!

143
00:17:27,980 --> 00:17:30,600
Time for you to pack
it up! They're closing!

144
00:17:36,480 --> 00:17:40,540
No, Kiku dear, you can't pay
the street tax, right, Pear?

145
00:17:40,840 --> 00:17:44,600
I've told you before, I'm
willing to help you with that.

146
00:17:45,260 --> 00:17:47,820
And all you have to do is marry me.

147
00:17:48,520 --> 00:17:50,520
You'd never have to work again.

148
00:17:50,760 --> 00:17:54,617
Plus, you can help yourself to all
the fresh food from the farm, P.

149
00:17:54,700 --> 00:17:57,560
I promise I'll make you a happy woman.

150
00:17:58,540 --> 00:18:01,340
But I'm far below your social standing.

151
00:18:01,680 --> 00:18:05,240
If you're not ordering anything,
then I ask that you leave.

152
00:18:05,980 --> 00:18:10,100
You think I would order anything
from this place? Come on!

153
00:18:10,300 --> 00:18:12,360
Eating dumplings made from scraps?

154
00:18:12,580 --> 00:18:14,580
What in places do you take me for?

155
00:18:14,840 --> 00:18:16,917
I would never stoop so low.

156
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:19,080
It would be an embarrassment, Peef.

157
00:18:20,660 --> 00:18:24,013
Did you forget that I'm a
famous Yokozuna at the capital?

158
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:33,580
I'm the greatest sumo
wrestler in the land of Wano!

159
00:18:34,660 --> 00:18:35,490
Urashima!

160
00:18:38,580 --> 00:18:41,260
Quit the tea house and come with me!

161
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:45,417
I can take you far away from
this poverty-stricken lifestyle!

162
00:18:45,500 --> 00:18:48,680
No more selling leftovers to get by.

163
00:18:49,180 --> 00:18:51,260
Think of how good you'll have it.

164
00:18:52,540 --> 00:18:53,370
Kiku!

165
00:19:01,820 --> 00:19:02,650
Tsuru!

166
00:19:04,960 --> 00:19:07,560
Tama drank the river water and fell ill.

167
00:19:09,140 --> 00:19:10,360
My goodness.

168
00:19:10,760 --> 00:19:11,780
Please, lady.

169
00:19:12,040 --> 00:19:13,500
You gotta do something.

170
00:19:14,140 --> 00:19:14,970
Kiku.

171
00:19:15,660 --> 00:19:17,600
Brew the evil purging herbs.

172
00:19:17,960 --> 00:19:19,300
Yes, right away.

173
00:19:20,040 --> 00:19:20,870
Hey!

174
00:19:21,780 --> 00:19:23,940
Just who do you think you guys are?

175
00:19:25,760 --> 00:19:28,000
Hey, big boy, move it.

176
00:19:30,940 --> 00:19:32,220
Shut your trap!

177
00:19:32,360 --> 00:19:34,242
I don't have to move for anyone!

178
00:19:38,700 --> 00:19:42,597
Kiku, I'll have a wrestling
match in Bekori Town today, Pei.

179
00:19:42,680 --> 00:19:47,160
I hope you'll come so I can
show you just how strong I am.

180
00:19:55,700 --> 00:19:57,080
Did we find them?

181
00:19:57,300 --> 00:19:59,360
It looked like the Straw Hats.

182
00:20:01,080 --> 00:20:04,727
Maybe I should go and talk to
them before there's any trouble.

183
00:20:04,920 --> 00:20:06,160
I don't know, Bepo.

184
00:20:06,720 --> 00:20:09,308
Nothing personal, but
you kind of stick out.

185
00:20:09,940 --> 00:20:11,657
Better luck next time, pal.

186
00:20:11,740 --> 00:20:15,269
Well, we should probably report
this to the captain for now.
